# ============================================================================
# 10-blink-core.patch - Blink core: screen, canvas, timing, fonts, geolocation, DOM.
#
# Part of the fp-fingerprint patch set. Apply in filename order:
#   00-core.patch -> 10-blink-core.patch -> 20-blink-modules.patch -> 30-webrtc.patch
#
# fp_config_helpers.h (00-core) is included by 32 of 36 files, so 00-core
# MUST be applied first. Any hunk mismatch aborts loudly; nothing is
# silently skipped.
#
# Regenerate with fingerprint/scripts/split_patch.js after adapting hunks.
#
# MERGE/UPGRADE GUIDE (new Chromium versions):
#   - Risk profile of this patch, counted from the per-file MERGE notes below:
#       8 LOW     (stable getters: screen, navigator hardware, perf timing)
#       8 MEDIUM  (occasionally refactored: geolocation, fonts, media values)
#       2 HIGH    (frequent refactors - expect manual hunk work):
#         * core/html/canvas/html_canvas_element.cc
#         * platform/fonts/font_cache.cc
#     Do the two HIGH files FIRST: they are the ones that decide whether an
#     upgrade is a morning or a week. If both apply cleanly, the rest is usually
#     mechanical.
#   - Every hunk here is an early return inside a getter, plus one #include of
#     fp_config_helpers.h. The include is the fragile part: Blink has been
#     actively migrating to fewer, more targeted includes, so an upstream change
#     can move a #include block without touching the function we patch. When a
#     hunk fails, check whether only the include moved.
#   - A silently-dropped hunk is the failure mode to guard against: the build
#     still succeeds and the key just stops working. fingerprint/scripts/check.py
#     catches a MISSING key, but not a key whose hunk was adapted into the wrong
#     function. After adapting, run the Client self-test, which compares the
#     reported value against the configured one per surface.
#   - Ordering: 00-core MUST be applied first (it creates the shared header).
#   - After adapting hunks, regenerate with fingerprint/scripts/split_patch.js
#     so the doc blocks stay in sync with the segments.
# ============================================================================

